# docker.thenairn.com — REMOVED 2026-08-23 (RAI-6). Proxied to
# `whatsupdocker:3000`. No `whatsupdocker` service exists in any of the 12
# compose files and no such container exists in `docker ps -a`, so this vhost
# has only ever returned 502 since the service was dropped.
# NOTE: five WUD_* variables are still live in `.env` (lines 55-59), including a
# GitHub token and a Slack token. Removing them needs Thomas — they must be
# revoked at source first. Tracked on RAI-6.

# pikvm.thenairn.com — 502, and the device is off the network, not misconfigured.
# Checked 2026-08-23 (RAI-6): TCP connect to 192.168.96.95 on 443, 80 and 22 all
# return EHOSTUNREACH ("No route to host") — the router has no ARP entry for it.
# The control host 192.168.96.14 answers on both 80 and 443 from the same place,
# so the LAN path is fine and the pikvm itself is powered off or gone. Left in
# place deliberately: whether the hardware still exists is Thomas's knowledge,
# not something the box records, and this config is correct the moment it is
# plugged back in.
pikvm.thenairn.com {
    @internal {
        remote_ip 192.168.0.0/16 172.16.0.0/12 10.0.0.0/8
    }
    handle {
        import admin
        reverse_proxy 192.168.96.95:443 {
            transport http {
                tls_insecure_skip_verify
            }
        }
    }
    handle @internal {
        reverse_proxy 192.168.96.95:443 {
            transport http {
                tls_insecure_skip_verify
            }
        }
    }
}

